  "title": "Forward metrics and finished output retain their rank, timing and beam gates",
  "mechanism": "Forward-pass metrics initialization is conditional on observability enablement, attention-TP rank zero and the final PP rank. This initialization always installs or reuses a DeviceTimer and sets _fpm_uses_device_timer true. The emit method contains a monotonic fallback, but the shown normal initialization does not make that fallback reachable; a zero accumulated device time suppresses emission. Output-stream acceptance applies its beam gate before its finished-request branch, so only a finished beam leader passes that gate. Nonterminal streaming uses unsent-token thresholds and may suppress a stop-string prefix. Ordinary full-pool usage subtracts both available and evictable capacity; the shown hybrid-SWA statistics path additionally clamps full and SWA usage when HiSparse is enabled.",
  "corrections": [
    "Do not describe the monotonic fallback as an observed normal FPM execution path.",
    "Finished requests are still subject to the earlier beam gate.",
    "HiSparse clamping in the hybrid-SWA statistics path is not a universal clamp on all pool-reporting functions."
  ],
